teacher_answer:
The composition of an odd function with itself results in an odd function. 

Given that \( f(x) \) is odd, we have \( f(-x) = -f(x) \). Then, \( f(f(-x)) = f(-f(x)) = -f(f(x)) \) because \( f \) is odd. Therefore, \( f(f(x)) \) satisfies the condition for being odd.

Answer: \boxed{\text{odd}}

